{"cut_proposal":{"candidate_errors":[],"prefix":"To solve the problem, we start with the given equation:\n\\[\n\\log_2 (\\log_8 x) = \\log_8 (\\log_2 x).\n\\]\n\nFirst, let's introduce a substitution to simplify the equation. Let:\n\\[\ny = \\log_2 x.\n\\]\n\nUsing this substitution, we can rewrite the equation as:\n\\[\n\\log_2 (\\log_8 x) = \\log_8 y.\n\\]\n\nNext, we need to express \\(\\log_8 x\\) in terms of base 2 logarithms. Recall that:\n\\[\n\\log_8 x = \\frac{\\log_2 x}{\\log_2 8}.\n\\]\n\nSince \\(\\log_2 8 = 3\\), we have:\n\\[\n\\log_8 x = \\frac{\\log_2 x}{3} = \\frac{y}{3}.\n\\]\n\nSubstituting \\(\\log_8 x = \\frac{y}{3}\\) back into the equation, we get:\n\\[\n\\log_2 \\left( \\frac{y}{3} \\right) = \\log_8 y.\n\\]\n\nNow, we need to express \\(\\log_8 y\\) in terms of base 2 logarithms. Using the change of base formula, we have:\n\\[\n\\log_8 y = \\frac{\\log_2 y}{\\log_2 8} = \\frac{\\log_2 y}{3}.\n\\]\n\nSubstituting \\(\\log_8 y = \\frac{\\log_2 y}{3}\\) into the equation, we get:\n\\[\n\\log_2 \\left( \\frac{y}{3} \\right) = \\frac{\\log_2 y}{3}.\n\\]\n\n","prefix_end":937,"status":"review_required"},"eligible":true,"generation":{"generation":{"max_new_tokens":2048,"temperature":0.7,"top_k":0,"top_p":1.0},"ids":[1249,11625,279,3491,11,582,1191,448,279,2661,23606,510,59,9640,59,839,62,17,19788,839,62,23,856,8,284,1124,839,62,23,19788,839,62,17,856,4292,59,2533,5338,11,1077,594,19131,264,48968,311,39721,279,23606,13,6771,510,59,9640,88,284,1124,839,62,17,856,624,59,2533,16429,419,48968,11,582,646,18130,279,23606,438,510,59,9640,59,839,62,17,19788,839,62,23,856,8,284,1124,839,62,23,379,624,59,2533,5847,11,582,1184,311,3158,1124,11520,839,62,23,856,57758,304,3793,315,2331,220,17,89936,1011,13,79540,429,510,59,9640,59,839,62,23,856,284,1124,37018,35702,839,62,17,856,15170,59,839,62,17,220,23,27275,59,2533,12549,1124,11520,839,62,17,220,23,284,220,18,59,701,582,614,510,59,9640,59,839,62,23,856,284,1124,37018,35702,839,62,17,856,15170,18,92,284,1124,3